The 17-year global dataset exhibits an optical/$\gamma$-ray correlation with power-law slope $L_{\gamma} \propto L_{R}^{\eta}$ where $\eta = 1.67 \pm 0.02$ ($6\,\mathrm{h}$ bins) and $\eta = 1.60 \pm 0.02$ ($24\,\mathrm{h}$ bins). Individual flaring epochs show slopes spanning $\eta \simeq 0.4-2.0$, and Compton dominance $\mathrm{CD} =  rac{
